WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:03.280
More than maybe any other League of Legends player,

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:09.740
Enrique “xPeke” Cedeno Martinez is a man of two legacies.

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:14.300
One is his history as a player: one of the game’s most renowned,

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:17.480
from the earliest days of organized competitive play.

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:19.580
He has won incredible victories

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:24.620
(Casting)

00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:27.940
and won fans with his playful attitude.

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:35.380
The other is the organization he built: its rise from Challenger, to incredible competitive heights,

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:38.980
(Casting)

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:41.960
And then its disappearance in 2017.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:47.520
"It's really been a crazy story of what used to or what could have been a very successful organization."

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:53.240
With one firmly cemented and the other now in question,

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:59.680
the story of a mid laner who captured the imagination and excitement of a young esports audience

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:01.320
is more relevant than ever.

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:05.400
"Peke's a god, Peke's sh*t, Peke's the best, Peke's the worst, I have lived this so many times."

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.640
This is xPeke’s story.

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:17.400
Born in Spain on April 24, 1992, xPeke would rise to prominence during League of Legends’ early days.

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:24.380
While the game was officially released in 2009, it was in July 2010 that Season 1 began.

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:29.640
A ranked matchmaking queue that included a draft, it was where many early pros,

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:32.080
including xPeke, got their start.

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:38.460
Peke became known as a top laner on ladder, and would find his way onto oSk Gaming.

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:42.280
That lineup did well enough to be picked up by myRevenge,

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:47.820
but two months later, in March 2011, the squad was acquired by Fnatic.

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:53.020
Two months later, the team competed at the European qualifier for the first-ever

00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:58.640
League of Legends World Championship, scraping by as Europe’s third seed.

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:02.820
The main tournament saw three teams from Europe and North America

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:07.160
and a single team from both Singapore and Thailand face off.

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:10.920
But a travel issue caused xPeke to be late to the tournament

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:14.500
and the team had to use wewillfailer as a substitute

00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:20.820
Peke did rejoin the team after the first day and, while they had a rough start to the tournament,

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:24.640
Fnatic made it out of their group and marched their way through the bracket.

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:55.620
(Casting)

00:02:55.700 --> 00:03:00.640
The accepted meta of the game was still changing, and the tournament itself,

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:05.800
held at DreamHack Summer 2011 in Jönköping, Sweden, was dark and loud.

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:11.860
But regardless of how you view it in the greater structure of the modern LCS system,

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:18.220
it was a big deal back then. The game had World Champions: and Peke was one of them.

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:24.220
"Now I would like to thank my mom. Because I'm pretty sure she's watching me right now when it's so late..."

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:29.500
Fnatic played in a number of tournaments during  the latter part of 2011,

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:35.620
including a dominant, undefeated first place run at IEM New York which saw Xpeke

00:03:35.620 --> 00:03:38.800
move to the mid lane as the meta began to set.

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:43.640
(Casting)

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:49.500
The beginning of 2012 was a relatively quiet period for competitive League of Legends in the West,

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:56.740
but Fnatic were one of two western teams to travel to Seoul to compete in The Champions.

00:03:57.140 --> 00:04:02.340
The field was predominantly Korean and, left out of the World Championship,

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:05.920
it was an opportunity to test themselves against the region.

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:07.960
Though they made it out of the group stage,

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:13.580
Fnatic would fall to eventual third place finishers Team OP in the quarters.

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:27.220
(Casting)

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:33.140
Despite that, xPeke was already in the conversation as one of the best mid laners in the World.

00:04:33.140 --> 00:04:35.900
And he would soon have a chance to prove it.

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:42.640
In June 2012 Fnatic removed Shushei, and Mellisan left due to school,

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:46.680
so the team added sOAZ and Pheilox in their places.

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:52.720
Despite the moves, the team did not place high enough to make it to the Season 2 World Championship.

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:58.240
But the August 2012 announcement of a new format for competitive League of Legends

00:04:58.240 --> 00:05:01.520
would soon change the history of the game forever.

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:06.960
"Season 3 plans have been released from Riot. Going to be really exciting for the NA and EU scene..."

00:05:06.980 --> 00:05:09.640
"They're actually going to have two matches every week."

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:15.100
The league would hold qualifiers to admit the initial teams, and Fnatic got to work,

00:05:15.240 --> 00:05:18.400
playing in a number of unrelated tournaments in the interim.

00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:23.760
It was during this time that xPeke’s most famous moment took place.

00:05:23.820 --> 00:05:29.720
In the group stage at IEM Katowice, Fnatic found itself opposite SK Gaming,

00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:36.000
and xPeke faced down fellow Spanish mid laner Carlos “ocelote” Rodriguez.

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:42.820
"Fnatic vs SK Gaming goes back many many years. Are you aware of that storied rival?"

00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:46.880
"Yeah I'm aware, even in League of Legends we have been for like two years

00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:49.920
playing against each other already. So, it's a long story."

00:05:49.920 --> 00:05:55.440
After defending their nexus, it appeared that SK Gaming would march toward Fnatic’s base

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:58.860
and finish the job that their Super Minions had started.

00:05:59.240 --> 00:06:05.660
That is, until Peke provided us with one of the most memorable LoL moments of all time.

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:07.060
The xPeke.

00:06:07.060 --> 00:06:35.880
(Casting)

00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:40.920
xPeke’s rival and fellow countryman didn’t hold back his emotions in the post-game interview.

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:45.220
"I don't know man I don't know what to say. I'm really really destroyed."

00:06:45.220 --> 00:06:48.080
But xPeke was gracious in victory.

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:51.680
"Yeah the way you played today you're definitely a top team in the world."

00:06:56.300 --> 00:07:03.100
The inaugural EU LCS season began in February, and Fnatic made their mark on the league’s first split

00:07:03.260 --> 00:07:09.580
with a 22-6, first place finish en route to a grand finals win against Gambit Gaming.

00:07:09.580 --> 00:07:11.760
(Casting)

00:07:11.760 --> 00:07:18.320
(Casting)

00:07:18.780 --> 00:07:22.160
xPeke was also leaving his own mark:

00:07:22.380 --> 00:07:27.800
his personable attitude and tendency to joke around made him a celebrity in a league

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:31.080
that was just starting to choose its own heroes.

00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:33.300
"Welcome to the vlog of Peke."

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:35.640
"What are you cooking?"

00:07:36.520 --> 00:07:37.160
"You're mom."

00:07:37.460 --> 00:07:38.100
"My mom?"

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:38.600
"Yeah."

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:39.280
"Does it taste good?"

00:07:40.060 --> 00:07:41.380
"Can you tell us the story of last night?"

00:07:41.580 --> 00:07:43.020
"Well last night we..."

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:49.440
"Last night pretty much we wanted to get drunk and I just got one beer in four hours."

00:07:49.640 --> 00:07:52.280
"That was not the plan at all."

00:07:52.520 --> 00:07:56.500
"Why do you have a video of me naked. Why didn't you tell me. Why did you put that video in there."

00:07:57.520 --> 00:08:02.980
Peke continued his strong play into the summer split as the team took second overall,

00:08:02.980 --> 00:08:05.500
and then again won playoffs,.

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:14.820
(Casting)

00:08:14.820 --> 00:08:17.720
qualifying for Worlds 2013.

00:08:18.360 --> 00:08:23.580
With a dominant 7-1 group stage performance that saw them lose only to Team Vulcun,

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:28.580
Fnatic burst through the bracket, defeating NA’s Cloud9 2-1.

00:08:28.580 --> 00:08:32.580
(Casting)

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:38.400
(Casting)

00:08:38.400 --> 00:08:43.620
(Casting)

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:49.440
Of the six Western teams at the tournament, they were the only one to make Top 4.

00:08:50.080 --> 00:08:55.660
With AD Carry Martin “Rekkles” Larsson finally of age to play in the EU LCS,

00:08:55.660 --> 00:08:59.940
expectations for the team were higher than ever in 2014.

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:06.840
He moved to the starting roster in November, and the team then took a second-place finish at IEM Cologne.

00:09:06.840 --> 00:09:10.060
Fnatic did meet expectations in Spring,

00:09:10.180 --> 00:09:15.600
as they finished second in the regular season en route to yet another EU LCS title.

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:18.880
Qualifying for All-Star Paris as a result,

00:09:18.880 --> 00:09:27.580
Peke again found himself at an international tournament against a hot new mid laner: SKT Telecom T1’s Faker.

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:31.860
"It will be Kassadin for Peke."

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:38.460
"Faker Faker play maker. We've all seen the Zed highlight video. We've all seen what he did to Ryu.

00:09:38.540 --> 00:09:41.180
"He has locked in Zed once again."

00:09:41.260 --> 00:10:17.720
(Casting)

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:22.560
Faker would get the upper hand, and Fnatic went 1-3 in groups,

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:26.280
meaning they had to face SKT in the semifinals.

00:10:26.340 --> 00:10:28.080
They lost that series, too,

00:10:28.080 --> 00:10:34.700
but the crowd in Paris nonetheless chanted for them as they left the stage and the tournament.

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:47.260
While Summer 2014 got off to a rough start, the team rallied in the latter weeks

00:10:47.260 --> 00:10:51.840
took second, and roared into the playoff finals against Alliance.

00:10:52.120 --> 00:11:02.480
(Casting)

00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:07.840
Their second-place finish was good enough to send Peke to Worlds for the third time.

00:11:07.840 --> 00:11:14.340
But the task ahead of them was daunting as they shared a group with Korean first-seed Samsung Blue,

00:11:14.340 --> 00:11:19.440
Chinese third-seed Oh My God, and NA third-seed LMQ.

00:11:19.440 --> 00:11:23.380
“Do you kind of have a now-or-never feeling, approach to this tournament?"

00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:28.800
"Yes but you always have that feeling in every season. Even in season one I had this feeling already.

00:11:28.800 --> 00:11:32.340
That it's now or never if we don't win this season, I don't know what's next.

00:11:32.440 --> 00:11:37.500
I had the same Season Two, I had the same Season Three, I have the exact same feeling right now.

00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:40.320
Beacuse you don't know what's coming next, so it's always really scary."

00:11:40.400 --> 00:11:46.420
If it felt like the chance at a second Worlds victory for a Western team was slowly slipping away,

00:11:46.420 --> 00:11:48.300
this tournament confirmed it.

00:11:48.380 --> 00:11:51.340
"And there's so many individual mistakes from Fnatic here.

00:11:51.340 --> 00:11:54.640
Though xPeke had plenty of highlight plays in the group stage,

00:11:54.640 --> 00:12:06.160
(Casting)

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:10.340
Fnatic’s 2-4 record was not enough to get them out of groups.

00:12:10.340 --> 00:12:17.840
The only Western teams to make it out were Cloud9 and TSM, and neither fought their way into Top 4.

00:12:18.180 --> 00:12:24.740
The offseason brought big change for Peke as both he and Cyanide left Fnatic.

00:12:24.740 --> 00:12:32.180
But while the jungler was retiring, Peke had other plans. His second legacy would begin in 2015.

00:12:32.200 --> 00:12:36.880
"My name is Enrique. My ingame name is xPeke. I play for Team Origen as a mid laner."

00:12:36.880 --> 00:12:40.480
xPeke created esports organization Origen,

00:12:40.520 --> 00:12:47.780
and assembled a roster of promising talent with the goal of fighting through Challenger to qualify for the LCS.

00:12:47.780 --> 00:12:55.020
"I think I have been three or four years saying Fnatic pretty much and now saying I play for Origen feels...

00:12:55.020 --> 00:12:57.540
Feels really weird. Feels like I'm not even playing the same game."

00:12:57.540 --> 00:13:02.760
Like xPeke, top laner sOAZ was a veteran of the early competitive scene

00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:05.260
and had played with Peke on Fnatic.

00:13:05.280 --> 00:13:08.120
"It was a good opportunity to prove myself again."

00:13:08.120 --> 00:13:12.960
Amazing, the team’s jungler, had just come off a stint with North America’s

00:13:12.960 --> 00:13:14.160
Team SoloMid.

00:13:14.200 --> 00:13:20.680
"Even if they would be past their prime, they would still be better than 75% of players in the LCS."

00:13:20.740 --> 00:13:26.440
Mithy, the team’s support, was previously a member of Lemondogs and Ninjas in Pyjamas.

00:13:26.440 --> 00:13:31.940
He had been banned since June for toxicity, but with his ban now served,

00:13:31.940 --> 00:13:34.640
Origen offered him a chance at redemption.

00:13:34.640 --> 00:13:40.700
"I felt that the best way for me to start from scratch on a team with respected players and

00:13:40.700 --> 00:13:45.220
and show that anyone can change and I'm different."

00:13:45.300 --> 00:13:51.620
The team sought out Niels, who would later change his handle to Zven, as the team’s AD carry.

00:13:51.620 --> 00:13:56.920
"I even asked Rekkles, I remember. So I ask him, who do you think would be the best.

00:13:56.920 --> 00:14:00.840
and he told me, if you go with this guy Niels, I am pretty sure you guys will qualify."

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:04.020
And of course, Peke would hold down the mid lane.

00:14:04.020 --> 00:14:09.040
"Getting to LCS is the number one priority, for me it’s actually the only priority."

00:14:09.040 --> 00:14:11.640
But whether or not Peke was thinking about it,

00:14:11.640 --> 00:14:17.260
Origen was building hype and qualified for the Challenger Series with ease.

00:14:17.260 --> 00:14:20.160
Once there, they put up a 9-1 record,

00:14:20.160 --> 00:14:26.260
losing only a single game before rolling over Reason Gaming and Copenhagen Wolves Academy

00:14:26.260 --> 00:14:29.400
en route to the EU LCS Summer Split.

00:14:29.560 --> 00:14:38.400
(Casting)

00:14:38.400 --> 00:14:40.920
(Casting)

00:14:41.360 --> 00:14:47.640
And if there was any question about xPeke’s continued popularity as one of Europe’s legendary mid laners,

00:14:47.800 --> 00:14:53.720
that was settled when he appeared on the analysis desk for the EU LCS Spring Finals in Spain.

00:14:53.720 --> 00:15:03.120
"Peke! Peke! Peke!"

00:15:03.120 --> 00:15:07.200
While the hype was building for Origen’s debut and Peke’s return,

00:15:07.480 --> 00:15:10.960
it still wasn’t clear how they would stack up against the competition.

00:15:11.040 --> 00:15:15.100
"For you guys is there anyone you're specifically looking out for that you haven't played before?

00:15:15.100 --> 00:15:16.420
Or that you have played before?"

00:15:17.100 --> 00:15:24.360
"For me I'm mostly looking for Fnatic with Rekkles coming back to the team I think he's a really great

00:15:24.360 --> 00:15:25.900
addition for them."

00:15:25.940 --> 00:15:30.140
"To play against someone that you played with, because it feels so different when you play with people and then

00:15:30.140 --> 00:15:34.400
you play against them. You see stuff that you didn't realise or that they didn't do so.

00:15:34.400 --> 00:15:37.680
It's good to get a different point of view when you play against old teammates."

00:15:37.800 --> 00:15:45.560
Was this team legit, or were they simply a mix of veteran experience and upcoming skill trouncing challenger?

00:15:45.560 --> 00:15:52.020
As Fnatic put up an undefeated 18-0 season, Origen proved that they, too,

00:15:52.020 --> 00:15:54.200
were one of Europe’s powerhouses.

00:15:54.200 --> 00:15:58.460
(Casting)

00:15:58.460 --> 00:16:02.280
(Casting)

00:16:02.280 --> 00:16:06.600
(Casting

00:16:06.600 --> 00:16:10.620
(casting)

00:16:10.620 --> 00:16:14.700
(Casting)

00:16:14.700 --> 00:16:18.120
(Casting)

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:21.820
(Casting)

00:16:21.820 --> 00:16:23.540
In the playoffs, they reached the final.

00:16:23.600 --> 00:16:32.320
"Origen or Fnatic, will be picking up game one in this best of five live from Stockholm, Sweden."

00:16:32.320 --> 00:16:33.940
(Casting)

00:16:33.940 --> 00:16:37.540
(Casting)

00:16:37.540 --> 00:16:44.240
(Casting)

00:16:44.240 --> 00:16:51.140
(Casting)

00:16:51.140 --> 00:16:56.240
(Casting)

00:16:56.260 --> 00:17:01.900
They handed Fnatic their first loss of the season, but Origen couldn’t close out the series,

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:04.380
falling in the fifth and final game.

00:17:04.380 --> 00:17:30.060
(Casting)

00:17:30.060 --> 00:17:32.680
But Origen could still make it to Worlds:

00:17:32.680 --> 00:17:36.340
all they had to do was win the Europe Regional Finals.

00:17:36.380 --> 00:17:42.460
After a close series against ROCCAT, Origen blew away Unicorns of Love to earn their spot.

00:17:42.460 --> 00:17:46.680
(Casting)

00:17:46.680 --> 00:17:54.740
(Casting)

00:17:55.620 --> 00:18:01.500
Origen had made it to Worlds, but it was clear that even as Europe’s third seed,

00:18:01.500 --> 00:18:05.620
the rest of the tournament field wasn’t expecting much from xPeke.

00:18:05.760 --> 00:18:09.840
"I don’t think we have to prove anything, because the fans have counting us out already."

00:18:09.840 --> 00:18:16.640
Origen were the underdogs in a group with LGD Gaming, Team SoloMid and KT Rolster.

00:18:16.860 --> 00:18:19.880
Not a single player from Origen’s roster

00:18:19.880 --> 00:18:25.540
had been highlighted in Riot Games’ pre-tournament list of the world’s Top 20 players.

00:18:25.540 --> 00:18:28.580
The rest of their group had 6.

00:18:28.800 --> 00:18:32.380
Even xPeke himself came under fire from observers.

00:18:32.380 --> 00:18:38.080
"Well xPeke's the worst mid laner in the group. Some people even say in the whole world tournament."

00:18:38.640 --> 00:18:44.040
But if xPeke was the weakest mid laner at Worlds, he didn’t play like it.

00:18:44.320 --> 00:19:00.200
(Casting)

00:19:00.200 --> 00:19:04.280
And if some analysts were expecting Origen to roll over and die,

00:19:04.540 --> 00:19:05.760
they were disappointed.

00:19:06.340 --> 00:19:11.660
Against LGD, Origen displayed classic xPeke and sOAZ shotcalling.

00:19:11.660 --> 00:19:29.500
(Casting)

00:19:29.500 --> 00:19:33.400
And Team SoloMid underestimated them at their peril.

00:19:33.460 --> 00:19:40.220
(Casting)

00:19:40.240 --> 00:19:45.160
Even so, could the team defeat Korean powerhouse KT Rolster?

00:19:45.200 --> 00:19:47.960
They answered that question with a statement victory.

00:19:47.980 --> 00:20:01.140
(Casting)

00:20:01.140 --> 00:20:05.400
An undefeated Week 1 against some of the tournament’s best teams,

00:20:05.400 --> 00:20:08.080
and on European soil no less.

00:20:08.160 --> 00:20:12.420
Origen had already shown that their veterans were more than capable

00:20:12.420 --> 00:20:14.780
of keeping up with the greatest in the world.

00:20:14.960 --> 00:20:21.760
"I never thought that we would be able to compete at Worlds. And if we actually got to qualify to Worlds

00:20:21.760 --> 00:20:23.420
I never thought we would be a contender."

00:20:23.580 --> 00:20:29.820
Their Week 2 wasn’t quite as successful, as they dropped games against KT and LGD,

00:20:29.820 --> 00:20:35.180
Their 4-2 record was good enough to enter the bracket as the group’s second seed,

00:20:35.420 --> 00:20:38.920
facing Flash Wolves in the best-of-five quarterfinals.

00:20:38.920 --> 00:20:40.240
"Flash Wolves or Origen."

00:20:40.240 --> 00:20:41.840
"I'm going with the Flash Wolves."

00:20:41.840 --> 00:20:44.120
"I'm giving it to the Flash Wolves."

00:20:44.340 --> 00:20:46.840
What followed was classic xPeke.

00:20:46.940 --> 00:21:05.080
(Casting)

00:21:05.100 --> 00:21:09.380
Origen went up two games in their series against Flash Wolves.

00:21:09.540 --> 00:21:16.620
Their opponents from Taiwan struck back, but Origen secured their spot in Brussels in game four.

00:21:16.620 --> 00:21:22.360
(Casting)

00:21:22.380 --> 00:21:29.200
Origen moved on to the semifinals where xPeke’s path to the finals was blocked by a familiar foe

00:21:29.400 --> 00:21:31.360
SK Telecom T1.

00:21:40.140 --> 00:21:45.020
While Origen lost Game 1, it seemed like they could contest the series.

00:21:45.040 --> 00:21:49.640
But after a Game 2 loss, Game 3 went out with a whimper.

00:21:49.640 --> 00:21:57.500
(Casting)

00:21:57.500 --> 00:22:03.580
No one would have expected Origen to even make it this far, but the loss still stung.

00:22:03.680 --> 00:22:08.260
And the European crowd made sure that their appreciation was heard.

00:22:08.260 --> 00:22:13.900
"Origen! Origen! Origen!"

00:22:14.600 --> 00:22:17.180
One split, an unlikely roster,

00:22:17.180 --> 00:22:23.080
and a trip from Challenger and their gaming house in Spain’s Canary Islands to Worlds semis.

00:22:23.080 --> 00:22:26.020
2015 had been a good year for xPeke,

00:22:26.060 --> 00:22:31.100
who had balanced his role as the team’s mid laner against his duties as owner.

00:22:31.740 --> 00:22:36.240
But in 2016, even after his own strong performance at Worlds,

00:22:36.240 --> 00:22:39.240
he decided it was time to start stepping back.

00:22:39.240 --> 00:22:43.680
The team announced a six-player roster that included mid laner PowerOfEvil,

00:22:43.880 --> 00:22:47.360
intending to split time between him and Peke.

00:22:47.480 --> 00:22:52.660
But in reality, Peke had already moved away from the game in a big way,

00:22:52.660 --> 00:22:57.660
playing only three games in the team’s 11-7 2016 Spring Split.

00:22:57.660 --> 00:23:01.580
"I still want to play. I hope I can do it sooner than later to be honest."

00:23:01.580 --> 00:23:04.320
The team again made it to the playoff finals.

00:23:04.360 --> 00:23:10.000
But Peke’s old rival ocelote had been busy assembling a roster for his own organization,

00:23:10.060 --> 00:23:11.620
G2 Esports.

00:23:11.740 --> 00:23:15.540
And Origen would again have to settle for second.

00:23:15.540 --> 00:23:19.400
"We lost against G2, 3-1.

00:23:19.680 --> 00:23:24.220
But really, felt really sad to go in play one game and lose."

00:23:24.220 --> 00:23:27.400
Origen did not improve in the summer.

00:23:27.840 --> 00:23:32.640
Both Niels and Mithy went to his old rival’s team, G2 Esports,

00:23:32.760 --> 00:23:39.340
and Origen signed veteran Greek AD carry FORG1VEN and Dutch support Hybrid to replace them.

00:23:39.500 --> 00:23:45.740
The team struggled early and FORG1VEN left the team after three weeks, citing problems with motivation.

00:23:46.140 --> 00:23:51.820
Peke chose not to replace FORG1VEN and instead played AD carry himself.

00:23:51.820 --> 00:23:55.980
And almost a year removed from a Top 4 finish at Worlds,

00:23:55.980 --> 00:24:04.460
Origen posted a 12-24 record and had to play the promotion tournament to retain their spot in the EU LCS.

00:24:04.460 --> 00:24:07.580
Origen stayed alive, just barely.

00:24:07.580 --> 00:24:18.080
(Casting)

00:24:18.080 --> 00:24:22.600
Heading into Season 7, the team’s roster was completely rebuilt,

00:24:22.600 --> 00:24:26.040
with only Peke remaining in the lineup as a substitute.

00:24:26.040 --> 00:24:31.480
They added Satorius, Wisdom, NaeHyun, Tabzz and Hiiva.

00:24:31.620 --> 00:24:36.180
But Peke watched as his dream, and the organization he had built,

00:24:36.360 --> 00:24:40.420
slowly slipped back toward the possibility of relegation.

00:24:40.520 --> 00:24:47.720
Peke again inserted himself into the starting lineup, this time playing support as the team released Hiiva.

00:24:47.720 --> 00:24:53.280
"xPeke he is an incredible player and he has a long and storied history.

00:24:53.280 --> 00:24:57.200
And now he's playing his third role on the LCS stage."

00:24:57.200 --> 00:24:58.660
It wasn’t enough.

00:24:58.820 --> 00:25:04.460
With a 0-13 regular season record, the team fell to the promotion tournament

00:25:04.500 --> 00:25:08.180
where they didn’t win a single game, and were relegated.

00:25:10.040 --> 00:25:14.640
xPeke’s legacy as a player and personality is firmly cemented.

00:25:14.760 --> 00:25:19.820
The backdoor play he popularized will likely bear his name forever in League of Legends,

00:25:19.900 --> 00:25:25.300
and his infectious personality and flashy style have made him a fan favorite.

00:25:25.560 --> 00:25:31.340
But his organization’s legacy is in jeopardy. In summer 2017,

00:25:31.340 --> 00:25:37.160
the team tried unsuccessfully to climb out of Challenger but then basically dropped off the map.

00:25:37.160 --> 00:25:44.360
Then, in 2018, the organization announced funding from soccer star Alvaro Arbeloa.

00:25:44.640 --> 00:25:49.140
They signed a number of veteran pros to compete in the EU Masters tournament,

00:25:49.340 --> 00:25:51.960
topped their group, and took the event.

00:25:54.840 --> 00:26:02.080
But can Origen, who captured the imaginations of so many EU LCS fans, rise again?

00:26:02.220 --> 00:26:05.560
It’s a question unanswered for the moment.

00:26:05.780 --> 00:26:14.020
Still, when the chips are down and he’s got that signature grin on his face, it’s hard to bet against xPeke.

00:26:16.200 --> 00:26:21.000
Thanks for watching. If you want more great content just like this, be sure to hit the subscribe button.

